\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Optimizer state and parameter update}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{pretraining}
\tag{optimization}

\p{An \newvocab{optimizer state} is a value #{s_k} retained between updates.
An optimizer is a map
##{
\operatorname{Opt}:(\theta_k,s_k,g_k)
\longmapsto(\theta_{k+1},s_{k+1}).
}
The map may also depend on a declared learning-rate schedule and update index.}

\p{Adam, for example, keeps exponential moving averages of first and second
gradient moments; see \citet{sec. 2}{kingma2015adam}. The Transformer training
configuration in \citet{sec. 5.3}{vaswani2017attention} specifies Adam and a
learning-rate schedule. The abstract map above keeps the persistent state
visible without assuming that every protocol uses Adam.}
